Match the Cellular Structure with its Function:
Cellular Structures:
A. Mitochondria;
B. Ribosomes;
C. Cell Membrane;
D. Nucleus
Functions:
1. Site of protein synthesis;
2. Control center of the cell, stores genetic information;
3. Powerhouse of the cell, produces ATP;
4. Regulates the passage of substances in and out of the cell
